 "title": "Public Records Request",
 "text": "Public Records Request\nSkip to main content Enable accessibility for low vision Open the accessibility menu\nes-exclude-start-header\nAn official website of the Cuyahoga County government. Here’s how you know\nThe site is secure.\nA lock or https:// means you’ve safely connected to the .gov website. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites.\nThe .gov means it's official.\nA .gov website belongs to an official government organization in the United States.\nSkip to Main Content\nTo Top\n-->\nA + A -\n-->\nSite Search\nSubmit\nFacebook\nTwitter\nYoutube\nNewsletter Registration\nInstagram\nPodcast\nToggle navigation\nServices\nBusiness\nGovernment\nCommunity\nDepartments\nToggle navigation\nHow Do I\nTopics\nApply For...\nCounty Job Opportunities\nChild Care Assistance\nMarriage License\nSenior Services\nGet Help For...\nAlcohol, Drug Addiction & Mental Health Problems\nFamilies & Children\nSeniors & Disabled Persons\nUtility Assistance\nVeterans\nFile...\nPublic Records Request\nLearn About...\nBid Opportunities\nConsumer Protection\nEmergency Preparedness\nFoster Parenting or Adoption\nHeroin Preventionme\nInmate Information\nRecycling Programs\nReport...\nChild Abuse\nConsumer Scams\nDrug Activity\nElder Abuse\nWanted Persons\nFind...\nDepartment A-Z Directory\nEmergency Services\nLost Dogs\nMaps & GIS Information\nMy Polling Location\nNeighborhood Family Service Centers\nPublic Notices and Bid Opportunities\nReal Property Information\nSexual Offenders\nRegister...\nAuto or Boat Titles\nBirth & Death Certificates\nPermits & Licenses\nTo Vote\nView...\nCourt Docket\nDeed Information\nElection Information\nForeclosure Sales\nMissing Persons\nReal Property Information\nSexual Offenders\nPay for.../Purchase\nChild Support\nCommissary Online for an Inmate\nDog Licenses\nProperty Taxes\nTopics full list\nResident Services\nsearch\nHome\nPublic Records Request\nes-exclude-end-header\nPublic Records Request\nThe Cuyahoga County Code and Ohio Revised Code gives the public the right to make requests for public records.\nPublic Records Policy\nPublic Records FAQs\nPublic Records Request Form\nAll records which meet the definition below are public records, unless exempted under section 149.43 of the Ohio Revised Code. There is no fee to file a public records request, however fees may be assessed in accordance with Cuyahoga County Code Section 106.06 and ORC 149.43. \"Public record\" includes any document, device, or item, regardless of physical form or characteristic, including electronic records, created or received by or coming under the jurisdiction of any public office, which serves to document the organization, functions, policies, decisions, procedures, operation, or other activities of the office.\nMedia\nIf you are a member of the media, please send your request directly to:\nJennifer Ciaccia at jciaccia@cuyahogacounty.gov and Kelly Woodard at klwoodard@cuyahogacounty.gov for all general requests\nOther related pages:\nBirth or death certificates ​\nClerk of Courts\nMarriage licenses\nPublic Records Managers\nSee other county topics and services for more information\nWas this page helpful?\nYes\nNo\nHow could we make it better? Leaving an email can assist us in troubleshooting the issue.\nSubmit\nCancel\nThank you for your feedback\nYour feedback means a lot to us. We use it to improve the experience of all of our users.\nes-exclude-start-footer\nInformation for\nResidents\nBusinesses\nVisitors\nContact Us\nCuyahoga County Headquarters 2079 East Ninth Street\nCleveland, OH 44115\n216-443-7000\nCounty Social Media\nPublic Records Request\nSite Info\nDepartments\nPrivacy Policy\nDisclaimer\nEEO Plan\nAccessibility\nInterim ADA Transition Plan\nVulnerability Disclosure Program\nPowered by the Department of Information Technology\nThe official government website of Cuyahoga County.\nQuick facts about Cuyahoga County from the U.S. Census Bureau\nCuyahoga County is a member of the National Association of Counties\nes-exclude-end-footer",
